00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.590 align:start position:0%
here's a take destiny 2's story has  vastly improved over time sure but the  witch queen expansion has the best  campaign in destiny history yeah that's  right better than the taking king better  than our revenge quest for cage six  better than any expansion in destiny 1  or 2 so far keep in mind y'all this is  just my opinion and not our official  review our excellent guardian phil  hornshaw will have a complete review on  destiny 2 the witch queen coming soon  like this vid while you're here sub to  the channel be prepared for some  potentially minor gameplay spoilers and  let's dive in  what makes the witch queen without a  doubt the best campaign in destiny yet  is the structure of each mission add the  hive lightbearers the legendary  difficulty and some incredible  environments the result is you have a  campaign that rivals the golden days of  doom and halo  compared to previous expansions bungie  has made a big leap in the way it builds  destiny campaigns see destiny campaigns  have historically suffered from being  disjointed and lacking cohesion  particularly with the first game bungie  moved in the right direction with the  taken king and destiny 2 definitely  demonstrated learnings from past  missteps and flex its muscles with each  major expansion  there have always been incredible  narrative wow moments with any expansion  but until the seasonal model really took  over most of the story threads felt  disjointed this has changed recently and  with the witch queen we're finally  seeing bungie melding together some of  its best destiny design with the  improved storytelling from its seasonal  model culminating together into a story  that is engaging still what you should  know is that fans of destiny have been  waiting for answers to several loose  ends created from taken king all the way  through vanilla d2's ending  on this front the witch queen definitely  delivers the goods although not without  some confusing moments in line's shore  but that is all okay though cause like i  mentioned earlier the new legendary  campaign is an absolute home run from  bungie  for starters the loosen brood is one of  the best changes to destiny enemies ever  specifically the lightbearer acolyte  knight and wizard each has the power of  guardian super such as blade barrage  sentinel shield and stormtrans and boy  do they pack a punch if you've had  crucible nightmares of swarm grenades  and guardian supers man that ish is back  to haunt you in the campaign there's an  added level of adrenaline when you  realize that light bearers are basically  the equivalent to guardians and that  they can respawn and come back to life  after you kill them there is nothing  more brutal than whittling down a  lightbearer's health just forget about  its ghost and see it resurrect right  before your eyes  there's another minor benefit of the  light bearers depending on your opinion  on champions but the lack of champions  in the campaign especially on legendary  difficulty to me is a welcome one the  lightbearers are clearly serving this  kind of champion type replacement and  for the better however except for the  overloads i still personally like  champions i think is a smart way to push  restricted loadouts as a type of  challenge in the nightfall strikes but  fighting champions forces you to cycle  through gear and requiring that in a new  expansion campaign that wouldn't have  been smart the reason being we're  constantly getting gear drops both rare  and legendary so it's only natural to  want to test out all the new goodies to  your disposal out in the field and not  only that but champions kind of force  you to take them on from a safe distance  which is fine and it's still tense for  grandmaster nightfalls but it's not what  i want from a story campaign  this doesn't mean that the light bearers  give you the full green light to just go  in guns blazing you still have to be  incredibly careful  once you start dueling light bearers you  are forced to risk leaving cover to  finish off their ghosts once and for all  this creates a clever layer of fighting  where you're not only cognizant of how  to take these mini bosses down but when  you should take them down  throw in the hive wizard's ability to  create a healing rift or the acolyte  smoking you out with its grenade and  you've got a genuine challenge on your  hands  i find the light bears to be a  significant change in creating an added  layer of difficulty that isn't only tied  to a gear check the extra challenge of  the light bearers combined with the  incredibly varied level design and the  major encounters they work together in  tandem and all of this ensures you were  constantly wowed always moving to  another location that feels fresh and  never able to get fully comfortable and  safe from your enemies  if we were to describe the campaign  purely from mission length a single  witch queen campaign mission would be  about as long as let's say two to three  older destiny missions across any past  expansion not to mention plenty of older  destiny missions were painfully  predictable and aesthetically plain  the witch queen doesn't completely  abandon the core loop of traveling  across the expansion's new location  exploring areas fighting minions and a  potential boss but it doesn't prove it  the difficulty for the legendary  campaign scales meaning the more people  there are in your fire team the more  enemies will spawn bosses will also be  tankier and have way more health go solo  and you'll still be pushed and  challenged but with less overwhelming  odds this extra difficulty is not only  welcome but has a reward incentive  each mission has several major  encounters and completing these  encounters will give you two loot chests  seeing these chests spawn after a  particularly stressful boss fight feels  awesome and it's nice to know that the  game is respecting your time choosing  the harder fight so overall the rewards  feel appropriate  there's also an incredibly challenging  revive mechanic if you decide to take on  the legendary difficulty as a fire team  each guardian will only have one revive  token similar to how revives work in  darkness zones during the raids  once you revive a teammate you can't  revive anyone again during that fight  meaning jumping out of cover too often  or straying away from your team and  losing a token mid-fight can come around  to bite you there's also a timer  countdown on each ghost when a guardian  dies forcing your teammates to act  quickly and trying to snag the revive or  get wiped and have to retry the  encounter  it all adds a hectic sense of urgency  that can snowball into pure chaos with  dozens of already souped-up minions and  bosses chasing you down all as you try  to avoid the wipe timer  the new major encounters are also a  radical change from past destiny story  missions and take inspiration from  dungeon or even raid mechanics but in a  far more manageable form  each mission has a couple of major  encounters it may be an arena fight  while adjusting a cannon or completing a  ghost scan or battling hordes of enemies  while trying to unlock a sealed path to  your objective  meanwhile the parts between these  encounters involve a really interesting  amount of platforming that uses a new  deep sight system deep sight resonance  is basically the ability to see hidden  platforms or clues in the area for a  limited amount of time you activate it  at clearly visible spots and have about  a 30 second timer to find what you're  looking for or to cross the platforms  that it reveals adding an extra layer of  urgency to progress  deep side also makes the world feel  alive as you notice parts that were  formerly hidden such as footsteps on the  ground giving you hints on where to  search or seeing statues suddenly  pointing indicating you're on the right  path  lastly i have to gush about the visual  look of this campaign it is so damn good  for you eldon ring and from soft fans  yeah power yourself on the back the  aesthetic of those games are amazing and  their influence is clearly seen in the  hive architecture of salvation's throne  world i mean just  come on  in fact now is a good time to mention  that the areas in this campaign are  incredibly varied despite all being  situated primarily on salvathun's throne  world alongside current destiny 2  locations in fact it is so diverse  that all the footage you have seen so  far in this video has only been from the  first few campaign missions and this  doesn't even come close to scratching  the surface of some of the surprises  waiting in store in the second half of  the campaign  everything about this campaign has left  me in awe the revamped level design is  incredible the difficulty of the  legendary edition and the excellent  rewards feel great the loose and brood  the story beats the platforming the  puzzles the witch queens campaign just  feels complete  i can't believe i'm saying it but it  does  there was always something missing from  older destiny campaigns that felt like  you were going through the motions to  hit the end game as fast as possible not  really caring for what was going on in  the game world and just hoping to get to  the great gameplay of raids and dungeons  to be honest i went into witch queen  optimistic but ultimately expecting the  same so i was so caught off guard and so  happy that i deliberately paused and  took my time taking in every cutscene  interaction and major encounter guys i  literally didn't sleep the first day i  couldn't this felt like a triumphant  home run of a campaign and the only  frustration i have is that i need to  know what happens next in the story  right now  destiny 2 the witch queen is out and  we've got an excellent video breaking  down why it's a great time to play  destiny right now on our channel fans of  the game be sure to check out  gamespot.com that is where almost all of  our destiny content is at from guides to  breaking news especially deep dive lore  breakdowns and story catch-ups stay  tuned for our official destiny 2 review  by phil hornshaw in the coming weeks and  check out our game spot after dark  podcast as we'll have a spoiler cast  story breaking down discussions with  myself phil and jean-luc until next time  guardian  you
 

